From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:07:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 106/117] docs(formulas): say what self-review actually runs
 (gcp-et7g.1, gcp-eief part 1)

The self-review step claimed more than it does. Its title said
"(affected-aware)", its heading and else-branch said the fallback runs "the
full suite", and its closing paragraph said "the rig's CI will run the same
affected subset". None of that holds everywhere: on winnow test_command is
`gate.sh test`, which already selects by diff, and winnow CI has no
pull_request trigger at all.

The title is now "Self-review and run tests". The heading names
affected_tests_command when the rig sets one, else test_command as the rig
configured it (which may itself select by diff), and the else-branch comment
says the same. The closing paragraph now makes the claim that is true on
every rig: a change that fails locally fails again downstream, at the
refinery gate or in CI.

Wording only; the commands the step runs are unchanged. Rides this bead per
Hunter (2026-09-27): same file, same pin move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
index 9cac73dc..03f28e26 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
@@ -352,7 +352,7 @@ on the bead."""
 
 [[steps]]
 id = "self-review"
-title = "Self-review and run tests (affected-aware)"
+title = "Self-review and run tests"
 needs = ["implement"]
 description = """
 Review your changes and verify they work. Override of mol-polecat-base
@@ -386,7 +386,8 @@ debug cruft, unintended file changes. Fix anything you find.
 {{build_command}}
 ```
 
-**3. Run tests — affected subset if rig provides one, full suite otherwise:**
+**3. Run tests — the rig's `affected_tests_command` when it sets one, else its
+`test_command` as configured (which may itself select by diff):**
 ```bash
 if [ -n "{{affected_tests_command}}" ]; then
     # Rig has an affected-tests detector. Run only the tests our diff
@@ -395,7 +396,9 @@ if [ -n "{{affected_tests_command}}" ]; then
     # internally and execute the relevant test subset.
     {{affected_tests_command}}
 else
-    # No affected detector — run the full suite (legacy behavior).
+    # No affected detector — run test_command as the rig configured it.
+    # That is not necessarily the full suite: a rig's test_command may
+    # itself select by diff.
     {{test_command}}
 fi
 ```
@@ -403,10 +406,9 @@ fi
 **ALL CHECKS MUST PASS.** If your change caused the failure, fix it.
 If pre-existing, file a bead.
 
-Refusing to push on local failure is a feature: the rig's CI will run the
-same affected subset (and more), and a PR that already fails locally will
-fail in CI too — wasting reviewer attention and CI minutes. Fix before
-submitting.
+Refusing to push on local failure is a feature: a change that fails locally
+fails again downstream, at the refinery gate or in CI — wasting reviewer
+attention and gate time. Fix before submitting.
 
 **4. Ensure everything is committed:**
 ```bash
